TY  - JOUR
TI  - A role for universal pension? Simulating universal pensions in Ecuador, Ghana, Tanzania and South Africa
AU  - Jouste, Maria
AU  - Rattenhuber, Pia
VL  - 12
IS  - 1
PY  - 2019
DA  - 2019/04/30
SP  - 13-51
C1  - IJM 2019;12(1):13-51
DO  - 10.34196/ijm.00193
UR  - https://doi.org/10.34196/ijm.00193
AB  - We use four novel, cross-country comparable tax-benefit microsimulation models for Ecuador, Ghana, Tanzania and South Africa to analyse ex ante the expansion of a universal old-age pension in a static setting. Universal pensions would significantly reduce poverty and inequality in settings where no means-tested old-age pensions exist (such as in Ghana and Tanzania). If means-tested old-age pensions exist and shall be maintained, universal pensions as a top up scheme only make a difference for the income distribution if the existing schemes do not reach the entire vulnerable population such as in Ecuador. Costs for the proposed schemes are substantial.
KW  - tax-benefit microsimulation
